7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Hi everyone. We've designed Burp AI with a strong focus on data privacy and responsible data handling.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
When using AI features in Burp, data collected from Burp Suite Pro is sent through our Burp AI platform to interact with one or more LLMs.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Importantly, we have zero data retention agreements with the third party model providers.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
So anything sent to them can't be stored or used to train their models.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
On our platform, we only keep data as needed to make the service work.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Like for maintaining stateful conversations with LLMs.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,000
We treat all data as unstructured by default, meaning we don't actively interpret or categorise it.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:20,000
While we don't actively analyse this data, if we spot sensitive information during maintenance and support, we're required to delete it to stay ISO compliant.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:28,000
If you can't use AI for a specific client engagement, you can disable Burp AI on a per project basis in Burp Pro settings.

16
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
This ensures no data is sent to Burp AI while that project file is loaded.

